[delegate] translator <- Repair target/src/lib.rs (crate `ulidgen`, batch-1 core generator) so same-millisecond ULIDs are strictly increasing in the random part, per the frozen contract in analysis/brief.md. The tester found that ulidgen_r() re-randomizes the last 16 chars from fresh entropy on every call, so two calls within the same millisecond are not guaranteed to sort after each other (failing tests: test_same_ms_inplace_increment, test_wrap_restart_stays_unique_and_sorted). Fix: track the previously generated ULID (e.g. a static/OnceLock<Mutex<...>> or thread-local holding the last 16 random chars + timestamp); when the current timestamp equals the previous one, increment the previous random part by 1 (base-32 carry) instead of drawing fresh entropy, and only fall back to fresh entropy when the timestamp advances or the random part overflows (in which case advance the timestamp and restart the random part, preserving the existing loop/re-fetch behavior). Preserve the public surface exactly: `pub fn ulidgen_r() -> Result<String, UlidError>`, `pub const B32_ALPHABET: &str`, `pub enum UlidError` with Display/Error impls, and all seven gap mappings (getrandom+Result, 26-char String return, [10..] slice indexing, B32_ALPHABET.find, Duration::from_nanos(1_234_567), recursion→loop, const &str alphabet). Do NOT modify src/main.rs, Cargo.toml, README.md, or target/tests/ulid.rs. Before reporting done, confirm `cargo build --offline` succeeds and that two consecutive ulidgen_r() calls within the same millisecond return a strictly increasing pair (second sorts after first), and that `cargo test --offline` in target/ now passes all 8 tests.
